.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx price\-lists prices bulk\-update"
Upsert prices of a price list in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx price\-lists prices bulk\-update PRICE_LIST_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the prices in \fB\-\-file\fR in the price list PRICE_LIST_ID, a JSON array of prices, each with its id, or creates those that do not exist (an upsert). An item that failed with 500 may be one whose metadata.version is stale: Emporix reports it so, not as 409 Conflict. Read it again before you retry it. PRICE_LIST_ID is the ID that \fBepx price\-lists list\fR shows.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
