.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx price\-lists prices create"
Create a price of a price list.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx price\-lists prices create PRICE_LIST_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Adds the price in \fB\-\-file\fR to the price list PRICE_LIST_ID, in its currency: a JSON object with itemId (itemType and id) and tierValues: the id of each tier of the price model that priceModelId names, as \fBepx price\-models get ID \-o json\fR prints it, with a priceValue, e.g. \fB{"itemId": {"itemType": "PRODUCT", "id": "100200"}, "priceModelId": "pm1", "tierValues": [{"id": "t1", "priceValue": 15.90}]}\fR. Without an id, Emporix makes one, which the response gives. PRICE_LIST_ID is the ID that \fBepx price\-lists list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
